   - Ethanoic acid (CH3COOH): C2H6O3 + 3O2 → 2CO2 + 3H2O
   - Ethethanol (C2H5OH): C2H6O + 3O2 → 2CO2 + 2H2O

2. **Calculate the enthalpy change for the combustion of each compound**:
   - For ethanol:
     \[
     \Delta H_{\text{comb. of Ethanol}} = -1367 \text{ kJ/mol}
     \]
   - For ethanoic acid:
     \[
     \Delta H_{\text{comb. of Ethanoic acid}} = 2 \times \Delta H_{\text{comb. of CO2}} + 3 \times \Delta H_{\text{comb. of H2O}} = 2 \times (-393.5) + 3 \times (-285.8) = -787 - 857.4 = -1644.4 \text{ kJ/mol}
     \]

3. **Write the combustion equation for ethanol:**
   \[
   \text{C}_2\text{H}_6\text{O} + 3\text{O}_2 \rightarrow 2\text{CO}_2 + 2\text{H}_2\text{O}
   \]
   \[
   \Delta H_{\text{comb. of Ethanol}} = 2 \times \Delta H_{\text{comb. of CO2}} + 2 \times \Delta H_{\text{comb. of H2O}} = 2 \times (-393.5) + 2 \times (-285.8) = -787 - 571.6 = -1358.6 \text{ kJ/mol}
   \]
   (Note: The given value of -1367 kJ/mol is slightly different from this calculation, but we use the given value for consistency.)

4. **Write the reaction for the formation of ethanoic acid:**
