The pressure of the reaction process should be optimized to ensure the reaction proceeds at the desired rate and to avoid unwanted side reactions. The pressure should be high enough to ensure the reactants and products remain in the desired state but not too high to cause excessive pressure drop or to lead to unwanted side reactions.

