4. Substituting \( m = f'(a) \) and \( (x_1, y_1) = (a, f(a)) \) into the point-point form gives:
   \[
   y - f(a) = f'(a)(x - a)
   \]

This equation represents the line tangent to the graph of \( f \) at \( (a, f(a)) \). 

