\]
However, the correct ratio is \( \frac{s_1}{s_2} = \frac{3}{1} \), so \( s_1 = 3s_2 \). Substituting \( s_1 = 3 \), we get \( 3 = 3s_2 \), which gives \( s_2 = 1 \).

The volume of the second cube is \( V_2 = s_2^3 = 1^3 = 1 \).

