   To cover the distance of 30 km at a relative speed of 10 kmph, b will take:  
   \[
   \text{Time} = \frac{\text{Distance}}{\text{Relative speed}} = \frac{30 \text{ km}}{10 \text{ kmph}} = 3 \text{ h}
   \]

4. **Distance from start**:  
   Since b cycles at 20 kmph, the distance b covers in 3 hours is:  
   \[
   \text{Distance} = \text{Speed} \times \text{Time} = 20 \text{ kmph} \times 3 \text{ h} = 60 \text{ km}
   \]

