\[
Q^2 = \left( \frac{p_f c - p_i c}{c} \right)^2 + \left( \mathbf{p}_f - \mathbf{p}_i \right)^2
\]

Simplify further:

\[
Q^2 = (p_f - p_i)^2 + \left( \mathbf{p}_f - \mathbf{p}_i \right)^2
\]

Since \( (p_f - p_i)^2 \) is the square of a vector, it can be expanded as:

\[
(p_f - p_i)^2 = \left( \mathbf{p}_f - \mathbf{p}_i \right) \cdot \left( \mathbf{p}_f - \mathbf{p}_i \right)
