R = \frac{A}{A + B\lambda}
\]
where \( A \) and \( B \) are the Einstein coefficients for spontaneous emission and stimulated emission, respectively. The wavelength of the incident light is \( \lambda \). This is derived from the steady-state balance between emission and emission, leading to the steady-state intensity \( I \).

