- \( c \) is the speed of light, approximately \( 3 \times 10^8 \, \text{m/s} \).
- \( \lambda \) is the wavelength of the radiation.
- \( T \) is the absolute temperature of the black body in Kelvin.
- \( e \) is the base number of the natural logarithm, approximately \( 2.718 \).

This formula describes the spectral density of radiation, meaning it gives the power emitted per unit area, unit wavelength. 

