","(a) The force acting on the proton is given by \( F = qE \), where \( q = 1.60 \times 10^{-19} \, \text{C} \) and \( E = 500 \, \text{N/C} \).  
\[
F = (1.60 \times 10^{-19} \, \text{C})(500 \, \text{N/C}) = 8.0 \times 10^{-17} \, \text{N}.
\]  
Using Newton's second law, \( F = ma \), the acceleration is:  
\[
a = \frac{F}{m} = \frac{8.0 \times 10^{-17} \, \text{N}}{1.67 \times 10^{-27} \, \text{kg}} = 4.81 \times 10^{10} \, \text{m/s}^2.
\]  
The magnitude of the acceleration is \(\boxed{4.81 \times 10^{10} \, \text{m/s}^2}\).

(b) Using the kinematic equation \( v = v_0 + at \), where \( v = 35,000 \, \text{m/s} \), \( v_0 = 0 \, \text{m/s} \), and \( a = 4.81 \times 10^{10} \, \text{m/s}^2 \), we solve for \( t \):  
\[
t = \frac{v - v_0}{a} = \frac{35,000 - 0}{4.81 \times 10^{10}} = 7.28 \times 10^{-4} \, \text{s}.
\]  
The time it takes to reach a speed of \( 35,000 \, \text{m/s} \) is \(\boxed{7.28 \times 10^{-4} \, \text{s}} \).",fluency,"# Task Description
